1
00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:43,880
Aunt Da left Korn in your care
when he was just a baby?

2
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:46,560
Yes, since he was an infant.

3
00:02:47,160 --> 00:02:48,200
How many months old was he?

4
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:49,480
Six months.

5
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:51,320
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">But Korn was born in July.</font></font></i>

6
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:54,160
August, September, October.

7
00:02:55,920 --> 00:02:56,920
Was the report wrong?

8
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:58,920
Or was it a different child?

9
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:03,120
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Pimpa Tayawat, daughter</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">of Prajak Tayawat, owner</font></font></i>

10
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:07,400
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">of the multibillion-baht Tayawat Group,</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">has vanished without a trace.</font></font></i>

11
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:10,880
So…

12
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:14,360
the secret's still safe.

13
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:27,360
Sir.

14
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:03,640
I've just finished my work.

15
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:08,360
Did you need something
from Ms. Pimpa's office at this hour?

16
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,760
I just miss my daughter.

17
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:33,600
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Who got you pregnant, Nuan?</font></font></i>

18
00:04:37,680 --> 00:04:41,400
Spare me the tears. Tell me right now.

19
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:43,600
Who's the father of your baby?

20
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:45,960
I don't know, ma'am.

21
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:48,320
No!

22
00:04:50,360 --> 00:04:51,920
Tell me the truth!

23
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:57,880
You're hurting me, ma'am.
Please just fire me.

24
00:04:57,960 --> 00:05:00,760
I won't. Not until you tell me the truth.

25
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:03,200
Tell me. Who's the father?

26
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:07,280
Tell me! I said, tell me!

27
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:08,560
Let Nuan go.

28
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:13,480
I'm the father of her baby.

29
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:20,200
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">I won't listen!</font></font></i>

30
00:05:22,280 --> 00:05:24,520
How could you do this to me?

31
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:28,120
You owe your status today

32
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:30,840
to marrying me, don't you?

33
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:37,000
If my father hadn't let you marry me,

34
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:38,680
given you land

35
00:05:39,440 --> 00:05:40,920
and money to start a business,

36
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:44,360
could you have built all this?

37
00:05:45,400 --> 00:05:46,360
You'd still

38
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:50,880
be scraping by,
working as a laborer by the market.

39
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:57,320
-I was wrong. I'm sorry.
-End it with her.

40
00:06:00,440 --> 00:06:02,640
Nuan is carrying my child.

41
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:05,040
Tell her to get an abortion!

42
00:06:06,320 --> 00:06:08,280
Give her a lump sum as compensation,

43
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:10,240
then kick her out of this house.

44
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:12,440
I can't do that.

45
00:06:12,520 --> 00:06:14,120
Why can't you?

46
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:17,720
I love Nuan.

47
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,200
Get out!

48
00:06:23,880 --> 00:06:25,160
Get out now!

49
00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:28,320
You came with nothing. Leave with nothing.

50
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:30,840
If you love her so much,
take her with you.

51
00:06:30,920 --> 00:06:32,360
Get out!

52
00:06:32,880 --> 00:06:33,960
Get out!

53
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:35,960
I never want to see you again!

54
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:38,040
Get out!

55
00:06:50,320 --> 00:06:52,440
I rented a house with Nuan.

56
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:57,400
But we couldn't make it. We had no money.

57
00:06:58,280 --> 00:06:59,680
I couldn't do anything.

58
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:04,640
And I did something utterly vile
and shameful.

59
00:07:09,440 --> 00:07:11,960
I had no dignity left.

60
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:21,440
I'm sorry.

61
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,280
It was my fault.

62
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:28,520
Could you give me one more chance?

63
00:07:30,520 --> 00:07:31,960
Make her get an abortion

64
00:07:32,840 --> 00:07:34,120
and end it with her.

65
00:07:35,080 --> 00:07:36,080
Can you do that?

66
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:45,040
Mother.

67
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:49,320
Please forgive Father. I miss him.

68
00:07:53,520 --> 00:07:54,840
Well?

69
00:07:56,400 --> 00:08:00,360
If you do that,
I'll give you one more chance.

70
00:08:01,200 --> 00:08:03,320
Your last.

71
00:08:11,480 --> 00:08:14,240
Father, promise Mother you will.

72
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:20,600
The baby Ms. Nuan was carrying

73
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:22,640
was Ms. Nada, wasn't it?

74
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:25,840
Yes.

75
00:08:30,840 --> 00:08:34,240
You didn't leave her,
and she didn't get an abortion.

76
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:37,600
Did Mrs. Wasana believe you that easily?

77
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:43,440
She loved me so much.

78
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:49,360
She was counting the days
until I came back.

79
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:52,960
And a little girl

80
00:08:54,360 --> 00:08:56,400
knelt beside me…

81
00:09:02,560 --> 00:09:05,360
until her mother forgave me.

82
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:13,920
Ms. Pimpa really loved you.

83
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:17,520
I loved her too.

84
00:09:20,320 --> 00:09:22,520
But I was the worst father.

85
00:09:28,160 --> 00:09:29,000
Excuse me, sir.

86
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:35,360
You'd been inside a while,
so I came to check on you.

87
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:45,720
Sir, I think

88
00:09:46,320 --> 00:09:48,480
you should go home and get some rest.

89
00:10:30,520 --> 00:10:31,520
Come out, Korn.

90
00:10:58,520 --> 00:11:00,160
I went in to find evidence about Aunt Pim.

91
00:11:02,080 --> 00:11:06,120
The police initially said
she might have been killed in a robbery,

92
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,120
since her car and valuables were missing.

93
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:12,600
But I don't believe it.

94
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:19,560
What do you think Grandfather
was looking for in Aunt Pim's office?

95
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:24,480
I guess he just misses his daughter.

96
00:11:27,920 --> 00:11:32,800
You seem to understand him so well.
Must be the DNA you share with him.

97
00:11:38,120 --> 00:11:40,360
Are you really going to stop here, Korn?

98
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:43,720
When will you tell everyone the truth?

99
00:11:47,360 --> 00:11:48,200
Why?

100
00:11:48,880 --> 00:11:50,800
Do you want everything back, Wee?

101
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:56,680
And if I said yes, would you give it back?

102
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:03,280
But I won't take it.

103
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:06,000
As long as you want to keep your place,

104
00:12:06,520 --> 00:12:08,920
I'll keep all your secrets,
just like before.

105
00:12:15,320 --> 00:12:16,560
Thanks, Wee.

106
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:20,280
But can you do one thing for me?

107
00:12:21,920 --> 00:12:23,760
You have to tell me the truth.

108
00:12:24,560 --> 00:12:29,440
If you don't,
I won't be able to help you at all.

109
00:12:35,840 --> 00:12:39,040
Then can I stay at your place tonight?

110
00:12:40,120 --> 00:12:41,320
I want to see Alyssa.

111
00:12:41,920 --> 00:12:44,280
She's called me so many times,
but I haven't called back.

112
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:46,120
Of course.

113
00:13:26,200 --> 00:13:28,400
I'm sorry about Aunt Pimpa.

114
00:13:37,240 --> 00:13:38,560
I'm sorry.

115
00:13:40,560 --> 00:13:41,640
For what?

116
00:13:43,240 --> 00:13:48,000
For not answering your calls
or calling you back.

117
00:13:49,680 --> 00:13:51,480
There's been so much going on.

118
00:13:55,680 --> 00:13:57,960
I understand.

119
00:14:03,120 --> 00:14:05,000
Do you really understand…

120
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:09,720
or do you just not care?

121
00:14:13,440 --> 00:14:14,760
What do you mean?

122
00:14:16,760 --> 00:14:18,840
Well, I don't know.

123
00:14:19,360 --> 00:14:22,080
I just wanted you to worry a little
when you couldn't reach me.

124
00:14:26,080 --> 00:14:27,640
But you didn't seem to.

125
00:14:28,920 --> 00:14:31,280
You only called me once.

126
00:14:32,840 --> 00:14:35,760
Korn, is this really the time
to talk about this?

127
00:14:36,760 --> 00:14:40,680
There's never a good time.
You always shut me down anyway.

128
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:46,400
Seriously, Alyssa.

129
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:51,080
When will you be my girlfriend?
How long do you expect me to wait?

130
00:14:56,280 --> 00:14:58,560
Maybe when your last name is Tayawat.

131
00:15:08,120 --> 00:15:09,320
I'm kidding.

132
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:13,720
But honestly,

133
00:15:14,600 --> 00:15:16,840
my feelings for you haven't changed.

134
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:21,520
And like I said, you can wait or move on.

135
00:15:24,720 --> 00:15:26,240
So it's the last name?

136
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:28,800
What?

137
00:15:28,880 --> 00:15:31,160
That's what you want from me?

138
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:34,320
I told you I was kidding.

139
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:36,720
But I'm serious.

140
00:15:59,280 --> 00:16:00,640
Did you finish talking with her?

141
00:16:27,720 --> 00:16:28,680
Uncle Jak.

142
00:16:33,280 --> 00:16:34,720
How are you, my dear niece?

143
00:16:36,680 --> 00:16:38,320
What are you doing here?

144
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:42,920
Wait. Dad let you leave Tawan Island?

145
00:16:45,200 --> 00:16:49,040
I heard you closed a deal with Tayawat
worth hundreds of millions.

146
00:16:50,280 --> 00:16:51,240
Well done.

147
00:16:52,560 --> 00:16:54,920
Just tell me what you want.

148
00:16:57,720 --> 00:16:59,080
Won't you invite me in?

149
00:16:59,160 --> 00:17:01,360
No. We can talk here.

150
00:17:01,880 --> 00:17:05,000
Or would you rather wait for Dad?
I can call and arrange it.

151
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:09,200
Still as sharp-tongued as ever.

152
00:17:11,440 --> 00:17:12,720
With you doing so well,

153
00:17:14,160 --> 00:17:16,000
your father has nothing to worry about.

154
00:17:17,240 --> 00:17:19,480
Maybe he doesn't need treatment

155
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:22,520
for that stage-three cancer anymore.

156
00:17:24,079 --> 00:17:26,280
With such a capable daughter,

157
00:17:26,359 --> 00:17:28,200
he can die in peace.

158
00:17:32,800 --> 00:17:34,360
What are you talking about?

159
00:17:38,240 --> 00:17:39,640
Just as I thought.

160
00:17:40,800 --> 00:17:43,360
Your father hasn't told you, has he?

161
00:17:48,440 --> 00:17:52,880
The sale agreement for Tawan Island
is still in your name.

162
00:17:53,560 --> 00:17:55,320
Sign it over to me,

163
00:17:55,880 --> 00:17:58,480
and I'll leave you alone.

164
00:18:02,320 --> 00:18:04,240
Is everything alright, Ms. Alyssa?

165
00:18:09,920 --> 00:18:12,880
Wee, this is Jak,

166
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:14,240
my uncle.

167
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:16,840
Hello.

168
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:28,640
Let me talk to Dad first.
I'll get back to you.

169
00:18:41,760 --> 00:18:44,880
Is he the one who sent that man
to attack you before?

170
00:18:55,360 --> 00:18:56,280
Dad!

171
00:18:56,360 --> 00:18:57,960
He's been shot.

172
00:19:01,760 --> 00:19:03,760
Thank you for helping me.

173
00:19:06,320 --> 00:19:07,720
You should get inside.

174
00:19:11,120 --> 00:19:12,000
Okay.

175
00:20:12,240 --> 00:20:14,200
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Father, Mother, please don't fight.</font></font></i>

176
00:20:14,280 --> 00:20:16,880
Father, Mother, please don't fight.

177
00:20:18,600 --> 00:20:19,640
We need to talk this through.

178
00:20:22,240 --> 00:20:23,760
How could you do this to me?

179
00:20:23,840 --> 00:20:27,600
Why shouldn't I? You lied to me first.

180
00:20:27,680 --> 00:20:30,760
You didn't leave her,
and she didn't get an abortion.

181
00:20:31,800 --> 00:20:36,600
The baby had already developed.
I'm not cruel enough to kill my own child.

182
00:20:37,760 --> 00:20:39,720
So you're going to make her
your second wife?

183
00:20:39,800 --> 00:20:41,120
Yes.

184
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:44,000
She's just a servant.

185
00:20:44,600 --> 00:20:46,840
You can't make her your wife and my equal.

186
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:48,360
Why not?

187
00:20:49,400 --> 00:20:53,600
Nuan respects me as her husband.
She makes me believe in myself.

188
00:20:54,200 --> 00:20:57,240
Unlike you. You're always putting me down,

189
00:20:57,320 --> 00:21:01,880
making me feel small and worthless.
That's how you've always treated me.

190
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:06,720
You're choosing her?

191
00:21:07,640 --> 00:21:10,760
Yes. I love Nuan.

192
00:21:11,560 --> 00:21:12,960
I want a divorce!

193
00:21:14,640 --> 00:21:16,000
I won't divorce you!

194
00:21:16,880 --> 00:21:18,400
I'll never divorce--

195
00:21:19,520 --> 00:21:21,000
Mother!

196
00:21:22,800 --> 00:21:24,560
What's wrong, Mother?

197
00:21:24,640 --> 00:21:28,160
Mother! Wake up and talk to me!

198
00:21:28,240 --> 00:21:31,760
Mother! Please, Mother!

199
00:21:31,840 --> 00:21:34,760
Mother!

200
00:21:34,840 --> 00:21:38,080
What's wrong? Mother!

201
00:21:38,160 --> 00:21:40,000
Mother!

202
00:21:40,080 --> 00:21:44,440
Please wake up and talk to me.
I can't live without you!

203
00:21:44,520 --> 00:21:45,800
Mother!

204
00:21:53,200 --> 00:21:54,040
Who are you here to see?

205
00:21:55,560 --> 00:21:58,080
I'm looking for Nuan.

206
00:21:58,680 --> 00:22:00,440
She used to work in Bangkok.

207
00:22:01,280 --> 00:22:04,800
She has a child, about 4 or 5 years old.

208
00:22:05,400 --> 00:22:06,360
Do you know her?

209
00:22:06,440 --> 00:22:10,000
Oh, Aunt Nuan is in her room.
I'll go get her.

210
00:22:15,440 --> 00:22:17,120
Aunt Nuan, someone's here to see you.

211
00:22:24,600 --> 00:22:25,640
Mr. Prajak.

212
00:22:25,720 --> 00:22:27,080
Nuan.

213
00:22:34,480 --> 00:22:36,160
I'm sorry, Nuan.

214
00:22:38,160 --> 00:22:40,840
I've come to take you and our child home.

215
00:22:41,880 --> 00:22:43,760
I'm not going anywhere.

216
00:22:45,520 --> 00:22:46,520
Nuan.

217
00:22:47,360 --> 00:22:51,480
It was my fault
I couldn't take care of you.

218
00:22:53,160 --> 00:22:55,720
But Mrs. Wasana has died.

219
00:22:57,400 --> 00:23:00,440
You can come home and live with me now.

220
00:23:03,240 --> 00:23:06,800
Mom, I'm hungry.

221
00:23:10,320 --> 00:23:12,040
Is she our daughter, Nuan?

222
00:23:16,080 --> 00:23:17,560
What's your name?

223
00:23:18,840 --> 00:23:19,920
Nada.

224
00:23:21,520 --> 00:23:22,920
You should leave.

225
00:23:24,120 --> 00:23:28,360
And don't come back here.
I'm no longer your wife.

226
00:23:28,960 --> 00:23:32,000
Nuan, I'll take you and our daughter home.

227
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:35,440
I'll take the best care
of both of you that I can.

228
00:23:37,320 --> 00:23:39,200
I can't go with you.

229
00:23:40,480 --> 00:23:42,080
I'm married now.

230
00:23:43,200 --> 00:23:47,520
You should leave.
And don't come back here.

231
00:23:48,600 --> 00:23:52,160
My husband loves me very much.
I don't want him to get the wrong idea.

232
00:24:19,240 --> 00:24:20,360
Nuan.

233
00:24:58,760 --> 00:25:00,720
Help! Fire!

234
00:25:00,800 --> 00:25:03,200
Fire! Help!

235
00:25:04,880 --> 00:25:06,600
Thong, get Nada out now!

236
00:25:06,680 --> 00:25:07,760
Wait here, Aunt Nuan!

237
00:25:07,840 --> 00:25:09,160
Take care of her!

238
00:25:58,920 --> 00:25:59,840
Father.

239
00:26:00,360 --> 00:26:04,240
Why don't you go home and rest?
I'll look after the guests.

240
00:26:10,320 --> 00:26:12,440
Korn, go with Grandfather.

241
00:26:13,720 --> 00:26:14,600
Yes.

242
00:26:17,320 --> 00:26:18,440
Rawee can drive me.

243
00:26:20,640 --> 00:26:23,920
Korn can stay
and help look after the guests.

244
00:26:29,320 --> 00:26:31,880
Da, take me to Rawee.

245
00:26:33,720 --> 00:26:34,560
Yes, Father.

246
00:26:58,560 --> 00:27:00,680
You can wait in the living room.

247
00:27:02,080 --> 00:27:05,440
Or if you want to go home, take my car.

248
00:27:07,920 --> 00:27:10,920
I'll wait for Ms. Nada
and Phakorn first, sir.

249
00:27:12,880 --> 00:27:14,040
As you like.

250
00:27:52,520 --> 00:27:54,560
Sir, Ms. Alyssa is here.

251
00:27:55,600 --> 00:27:57,760
Oh, Alyssa.

252
00:27:58,280 --> 00:27:59,840
Aren't you going to work?

253
00:28:00,360 --> 00:28:01,320
Hey.

254
00:28:03,840 --> 00:28:05,200
What's wrong?

255
00:28:06,400 --> 00:28:08,040
Why do you look like that?

256
00:28:09,440 --> 00:28:10,960
Did someone upset you?

257
00:28:28,240 --> 00:28:31,400
It's only stage-three cancer.
I can handle it.

258
00:28:31,480 --> 00:28:34,080
You know I'm still strong.

259
00:28:36,520 --> 00:28:40,920
Only cancer? If it's only cancer,
why didn't you tell me?

260
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:42,880
Why did I have to hear it
from someone else?

261
00:28:43,760 --> 00:28:45,000
Who told you?

262
00:28:46,960 --> 00:28:48,040
Uncle Jak.

263
00:28:51,560 --> 00:28:53,320
Did Mr. Jak contact you?

264
00:28:54,360 --> 00:28:56,680
He came to my house the other day.

265
00:28:57,960 --> 00:28:59,600
Who let him leave the island?

266
00:29:00,440 --> 00:29:02,000
I'll take care of it, sir.

267
00:29:03,560 --> 00:29:05,720
No need. Let's deal with this first.

268
00:29:05,800 --> 00:29:08,680
What did Jak say when he came to see you?

269
00:29:10,400 --> 00:29:13,200
He wants to sell the resort
on Tawan Island.

270
00:29:13,280 --> 00:29:15,240
He asked me to sign off on it.

271
00:29:16,560 --> 00:29:17,680
Sir.

272
00:29:18,480 --> 00:29:21,360
Land prices on Tawan Island
have risen sharply.

273
00:29:21,440 --> 00:29:23,480
Many locals have already rushed to sell.

274
00:29:24,880 --> 00:29:25,960
What do you think, Alyssa?

275
00:29:27,320 --> 00:29:28,680
Do you want to sell, Dad?

276
00:29:31,880 --> 00:29:34,360
I originally planned
to give the resort to Uncle Jak.

277
00:29:35,160 --> 00:29:37,880
But after what happened,
I changed my mind.

278
00:29:40,280 --> 00:29:43,440
If it was meant for him
in the first place,

279
00:29:43,960 --> 00:29:45,520
I'm happy to give it to him.

280
00:29:47,240 --> 00:29:48,800
Selling it might be a good idea.

281
00:29:49,320 --> 00:29:52,800
But put it in the contract that he
must stay out of our other businesses.

282
00:29:53,840 --> 00:29:54,760
Okay.

283
00:29:58,160 --> 00:30:00,720
But you have to promise me

284
00:30:01,600 --> 00:30:05,440
you'll tell me everything from now on.

285
00:30:06,040 --> 00:30:08,320
Starting with your treatment plan.

286
00:30:08,880 --> 00:30:11,960
Don't worry. I have Thamrong.

287
00:30:16,160 --> 00:30:19,640
You have me too, Dad,
in case you've forgotten.

288
00:30:22,440 --> 00:30:23,520
I'm sorry.

289
00:30:25,360 --> 00:30:29,520
I didn't want you to worry.
I can handle my own problems.

290
00:30:30,640 --> 00:30:33,000
I want you to enjoy your work.

291
00:30:33,600 --> 00:30:37,880
You're just starting out in life.
I don't want you tied down caring for me.

292
00:30:39,000 --> 00:30:41,000
You have to ask me

293
00:30:41,880 --> 00:30:44,280
what I want to do, Dad.

294
00:30:44,800 --> 00:30:48,720
Right now, you're what matters most to me.

295
00:30:49,440 --> 00:30:53,960
So promise you'll tell me everything.

296
00:30:55,120 --> 00:30:56,240
Alright.

297
00:30:57,520 --> 00:31:00,600
I'll be sure to report everything
to my daughter.

298
00:31:03,160 --> 00:31:05,200
But you need to rest too.

299
00:31:06,400 --> 00:31:09,520
You don't have to work anymore.
I'll take care of it.

300
00:31:11,120 --> 00:31:12,560
Would you like Thamrong to help?

301
00:31:12,640 --> 00:31:14,960
Especially with the sale agreement.

302
00:31:18,640 --> 00:31:22,480
No, thank you.
I have someone in mind who can help.

303
00:31:32,200 --> 00:31:34,920
Mr. Rawee, Sir is asking for you.

304
00:31:35,680 --> 00:31:36,560
He's asking for me?

305
00:31:36,640 --> 00:31:40,200
Yes. He wants you upstairs
in Ms. Pimpa's room right away.

306
00:31:45,240 --> 00:31:47,600
Hurry, Wee. Don't keep
Grandfather waiting.

307
00:31:50,640 --> 00:31:52,240
-This way, please.
-Okay.

308
00:32:13,880 --> 00:32:15,880
Korn, go with Grandfather.

309
00:32:15,960 --> 00:32:17,240
Yes.

310
00:32:17,840 --> 00:32:19,000
Rawee can drive me.

311
00:32:36,360 --> 00:32:40,320
So, what do you think about my suggestion?

312
00:32:42,040 --> 00:32:44,240
I don't quite have the nerve to do it yet.

313
00:32:44,320 --> 00:32:45,320
Huh?

314
00:32:45,880 --> 00:32:49,520
Why not? There's nothing strange about it.

315
00:32:51,520 --> 00:32:54,800
Using company money
for personal investments isn't strange?

316
00:32:56,240 --> 00:33:00,240
No. I did the same

317
00:33:00,760 --> 00:33:01,960
when I first started investing.

318
00:33:03,560 --> 00:33:04,680
Why not?

319
00:33:06,040 --> 00:33:10,200
That money will be ours anyway.

320
00:33:11,680 --> 00:33:15,120
If not today, then someday.

321
00:33:17,400 --> 00:33:20,440
We're just borrowing it for now.
What's wrong with that?

322
00:33:22,240 --> 00:33:25,320
Well, I'd like to think it through first.

323
00:33:25,840 --> 00:33:29,840
With work and Aunt Pim,
I've barely had time to think.

324
00:33:34,000 --> 00:33:37,200
That's why they see me as the black sheep.

325
00:33:37,720 --> 00:33:39,520
I've been too busy investing for myself.

326
00:33:40,360 --> 00:33:43,560
Hey. But trust me,

327
00:33:43,640 --> 00:33:45,120
it's worth it.

328
00:33:46,320 --> 00:33:48,920
Do you ever see me
bothering with the company?

329
00:33:50,120 --> 00:33:54,240
No, because I make my own money.

330
00:33:58,040 --> 00:34:00,520
How do I get started?

331
00:34:01,920 --> 00:34:03,720
You already have the authority
to sign checks.

332
00:34:04,760 --> 00:34:06,400
If you can't take the plunge today,

333
00:34:07,160 --> 00:34:09,560
keep staring at that tiny stock portfolio.

334
00:34:11,159 --> 00:34:16,480
Remember, less capital means less profit.

335
00:34:18,440 --> 00:34:20,080
I'll get going, then.

336
00:34:20,960 --> 00:34:22,560
Time to spend some money.

337
00:34:34,840 --> 00:34:36,639
What were you talking about
with Mr. Panas?

338
00:34:41,440 --> 00:34:45,080
Nothing much. Just an uncle
and nephew chatting.

339
00:34:47,239 --> 00:34:50,800
Let me warn you, Korn.
Keep your distance from him.

340
00:34:52,639 --> 00:34:54,920
Don't worry, Wee.

341
00:34:55,440 --> 00:34:58,560
Uncle Panas is the only one in this house
who pays attention to me.

342
00:35:04,800 --> 00:35:08,520
Why did Grandfather call you over earlier?

343
00:35:10,080 --> 00:35:11,240
Nothing much.

344
00:35:12,320 --> 00:35:16,560
I guess he misses his daughter,
so he went to sit in Ms. Pimpa's room.

345
00:35:18,160 --> 00:35:20,360
Was there anything unusual
in Aunt Pim's room?

346
00:35:22,320 --> 00:35:23,720
What do you mean?

347
00:35:39,360 --> 00:35:43,560
Well, documents or anything like that.

348
00:35:45,640 --> 00:35:49,720
No. He just offered me a job
as an assistant.

349
00:35:51,240 --> 00:35:55,240
An assistant? Whose assistant?
His assistant?

350
00:35:58,960 --> 00:36:00,040
Are you interested?

351
00:36:01,480 --> 00:36:03,080
I already turned him down.

352
00:36:04,200 --> 00:36:05,480
Why?

353
00:36:06,680 --> 00:36:10,200
Wouldn't it be a good chance
to get closer to Grandfather?

354
00:36:10,800 --> 00:36:15,240
How could I leave you, Korn?
You brought me to meet Ms. Nada.

355
00:36:15,920 --> 00:36:17,200
Have you forgotten?

356
00:36:21,680 --> 00:36:26,440
I don't know.
Maybe I'm getting tired of all this.

357
00:36:28,520 --> 00:36:29,600
Korn.

358
00:36:31,440 --> 00:36:32,480
I'm sorry.

359
00:36:33,920 --> 00:36:35,280
For what?

360
00:36:37,280 --> 00:36:39,680
For how Mom and I

361
00:36:39,760 --> 00:36:43,280
decided to solve things
by having you take my place.

362
00:36:44,680 --> 00:36:46,720
I thought it would be good for you.

363
00:36:47,960 --> 00:36:50,120
But it's only left you

364
00:36:50,640 --> 00:36:53,920
feeling pressured and uneasy.

365
00:36:57,200 --> 00:36:59,920
That's why I said
I wish I'd never gotten sick.

366
00:37:01,360 --> 00:37:03,120
If you've had enough,

367
00:37:04,040 --> 00:37:05,720
you can always tell me.

368
00:37:07,640 --> 00:37:09,480
I'll sort it out for you.

369
00:37:14,160 --> 00:37:16,080
I'll talk to Mom about it.

370
00:37:19,760 --> 00:37:21,240
I'm always on your side, Korn.

371
00:37:45,000 --> 00:37:46,240
Here you go.

372
00:37:46,320 --> 00:37:47,640
Thank you.

373
00:37:49,960 --> 00:37:51,480
MOM

374
00:37:57,520 --> 00:37:59,000
Yes, Mom?

375
00:37:59,080 --> 00:38:02,440
Wee, I brought Somphit to Bangkok
to run some errands,

376
00:38:02,520 --> 00:38:05,120
so I brought lunch for you and Korn.

377
00:38:05,720 --> 00:38:08,160
Okay. I'll come down.

378
00:38:11,400 --> 00:38:13,520
-Yes?
-<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Wee, come into the office, please.</font></font></i>

379
00:38:13,600 --> 00:38:15,720
Sure. I'll be right there.

380
00:38:18,000 --> 00:38:20,240
Mom, I'll call you back.

381
00:38:21,000 --> 00:38:22,000
Okay.

382
00:38:46,040 --> 00:38:47,240
Hello, Grandfather.

383
00:39:01,800 --> 00:39:03,480
Why didn't you knock before coming in?

384
00:39:11,760 --> 00:39:14,600
I'd like to talk to you, Grandfather.

385
00:39:15,920 --> 00:39:17,480
Out with it.

386
00:39:20,280 --> 00:39:24,360
Why do you seem to value Wee more than me?

387
00:39:28,880 --> 00:39:31,480
Are you even my real grandson?

388
00:39:44,560 --> 00:39:45,720
Oh, Mom.

389
00:39:47,320 --> 00:39:48,160
Ms. Alyssa.

390
00:39:49,480 --> 00:39:53,520
I saw her standing downstairs alone,
so I invited her to come up with me.

391
00:39:54,120 --> 00:39:55,400
Thank you.

392
00:39:57,680 --> 00:39:59,400
Mom, you can wait in Korn's office.

393
00:40:00,080 --> 00:40:01,200
-Okay.
-Come on.

394
00:40:13,880 --> 00:40:15,080
Where's Korn?

395
00:40:15,800 --> 00:40:18,920
I'm not sure.
He was in here just a moment ago.

396
00:40:22,600 --> 00:40:25,200
Aunt Walai, I have to go to a meeting.

397
00:40:25,280 --> 00:40:26,360
-Goodbye.
-Thank you.

398
00:40:36,760 --> 00:40:38,920
Alyssa's lovely, isn't she?

399
00:40:43,560 --> 00:40:45,960
Is this really Korn's office?

400
00:40:46,600 --> 00:40:47,480
Yes.

401
00:40:49,960 --> 00:40:53,440
This should really be your office, Wee.

402
00:40:54,200 --> 00:40:55,640
It's all the same, Mom.

403
00:40:58,760 --> 00:41:01,680
Mom, I have to go. Taddao's calling me.

404
00:41:03,040 --> 00:41:06,520
Yes, I'm coming right now.

405
00:41:06,600 --> 00:41:08,120
Yes. Okay.

406
00:41:55,240 --> 00:41:56,880
I found this document

407
00:41:57,520 --> 00:42:01,080
in Pimpa's office. It's a DNA test report.

408
00:42:01,880 --> 00:42:03,760
You're not Nada's son.

409
00:42:05,520 --> 00:42:07,200
There must be some mistake, Grandfather.

410
00:42:07,280 --> 00:42:10,800
There's no mistake.
The results are this detailed.

411
00:42:11,600 --> 00:42:15,120
You knew Pimpa would uncover the truth.

412
00:42:15,200 --> 00:42:17,880
So you killed my daughter
to silence her, didn't you?

413
00:42:26,800 --> 00:42:28,960
You brat!

414
00:42:53,880 --> 00:42:57,800
A DNA comparison between Nada and Rawee…

415
00:43:00,600 --> 00:43:02,080
They're not mother and son.

416
00:43:05,560 --> 00:43:07,200
How can Wee not be her son?

417
00:43:17,240 --> 00:43:18,320
Mom.

418
00:43:19,760 --> 00:43:21,080
What are you doing here?

419
00:43:22,680 --> 00:43:25,120
What's wrong with him?
What did you do to him, Korn?

420
00:43:26,520 --> 00:43:27,480
Come with me first.

421
00:43:33,400 --> 00:43:37,320
Hey, Korn! What happened? I'm so confused.

422
00:43:37,400 --> 00:43:38,440
GENETIC ASSURANCE SYSTEMS

423
00:43:41,000 --> 00:43:42,640
You have to vouch for me.

424
00:43:42,720 --> 00:43:44,520
Say you were with me in my office

425
00:43:44,600 --> 00:43:46,240
and I hadn't been to Mr. Prajak's office.

426
00:43:47,520 --> 00:43:49,640
Was that Ms. Nada's father?

427
00:43:49,720 --> 00:43:51,680
What's wrong with him?

428
00:43:51,760 --> 00:43:55,880
-What did you do, Korn?
-Mom! Stay calm.

429
00:43:56,480 --> 00:43:59,280
We just had an argument.

430
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:01,720
It was all an accident.

431
00:44:03,000 --> 00:44:06,720
Will he be okay? Go help him, son.

432
00:44:07,720 --> 00:44:10,400
I will. But listen, Mom.

433
00:44:11,200 --> 00:44:14,080
I'm about to take you to meet Grandfather.

434
00:44:14,160 --> 00:44:17,960
You don't know anything
about what happened in that room.

435
00:44:22,680 --> 00:44:24,760
Go check on Mr. Prajak first.

436
00:44:24,840 --> 00:44:26,480
We don't know how he's doing.

437
00:44:31,480 --> 00:44:32,960
Sir!

438
00:44:33,040 --> 00:44:35,720
Sir!

439
00:44:37,880 --> 00:44:38,840
Sir!

440
00:44:39,640 --> 00:44:41,160
Wee, what happened?

441
00:44:41,880 --> 00:44:44,080
Korn, call an ambulance! Hurry!

442
00:44:47,320 --> 00:44:48,480
Yes, Phakorn?

443
00:44:49,000 --> 00:44:50,880
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Grandfather fell in his office.</font></font></i>

444
00:44:51,400 --> 00:44:53,920
What? Is he badly hurt?

445
00:44:56,680 --> 00:44:58,600
The ambulance has picked him up.

446
00:45:00,760 --> 00:45:01,680
I don't know.

447
00:45:02,320 --> 00:45:04,080
When I got to Grandfather's office,

448
00:45:04,160 --> 00:45:06,160
Wee was already holding him.

449
00:45:08,640 --> 00:45:10,200
You'll have to ask Wee about that.

450
00:45:11,320 --> 00:45:13,040
I'll be there as soon as I can.

451
00:45:14,280 --> 00:45:15,760
Is something wrong, Ms. Nada?

452
00:45:15,840 --> 00:45:18,040
Father fell in his office.

453
00:45:19,560 --> 00:45:20,920
Is he badly hurt?

454
00:45:21,000 --> 00:45:23,960
I don't know.
He's on his way to the hospital.

455
00:45:24,040 --> 00:45:25,560
Is anyone with him?

456
00:45:25,640 --> 00:45:28,840
Rawee is. Phakorn is on his way.

457
00:45:29,360 --> 00:45:31,640
Alyssa, I have to go.

458
00:45:31,720 --> 00:45:33,600
-Let me call Rawee first.
-Okay.

459
00:45:50,640 --> 00:45:53,240
Will Wee get into trouble
because of what you said?

460
00:45:56,400 --> 00:45:58,720
Would you rather I got into trouble, Mom?

461
00:46:02,240 --> 00:46:06,440
Wee is his real grandson.
He'll help Wee no matter what.

462
00:46:09,760 --> 00:46:13,440
Besides, Wee didn't hurt Grandfather.
What could anyone blame him for?

463
00:46:20,240 --> 00:46:24,280
I'm your son, Mom. Wee isn't.

464
00:46:25,640 --> 00:46:27,760
He's already safe.

465
00:46:28,360 --> 00:46:31,000
You have to help me before anyone else.

466
00:46:33,200 --> 00:46:34,360
Please, Mom.

467
00:47:08,520 --> 00:47:12,880
A DNA comparison between Nada and Rawee…

468
00:47:15,600 --> 00:47:17,120
They're not mother and son.

469
00:47:20,480 --> 00:47:22,120
How can Wee not be her son?

470
00:47:36,880 --> 00:47:39,400
I wonder if the police will suspect Wee.

471
00:47:43,520 --> 00:47:48,280
Mom, when Wee was little,
did you ever leave him with anyone else?

472
00:47:49,800 --> 00:47:53,560
No. I was afraid he'd be hurt.

473
00:47:53,640 --> 00:47:57,000
Your dad and I took turns caring for him.
We never let him out of our sight.

474
00:47:58,360 --> 00:48:00,240
We cared for him
even better than our own son.

475
00:48:04,920 --> 00:48:07,200
Why do you ask?

476
00:48:08,520 --> 00:48:09,920
It's nothing, Mom.

477
00:48:17,080 --> 00:48:19,960
Wee, what did the police say?

478
00:48:20,960 --> 00:48:25,120
They want me to get examined
to see if I have any bruises.

479
00:48:25,640 --> 00:48:27,080
They suspect I might have hurt him.

480
00:48:28,600 --> 00:48:31,560
That's good, son.
It'll help prove your innocence.

481
00:48:32,240 --> 00:48:35,800
They'll examine him too,
in case they find other evidence,

482
00:48:35,880 --> 00:48:39,160
like skin under his fingernails
or fingerprints.

483
00:48:40,880 --> 00:48:43,720
An old man falls,
and suddenly it's a murder case?

484
00:48:44,920 --> 00:48:49,160
They have to consider that possibility.
So much has happened to his family lately.

485
00:48:49,680 --> 00:48:54,040
First, Ms. Nada was shot,
then Ms. Pimpa was killed in a robbery,

486
00:48:54,640 --> 00:48:56,240
and now this has happened to him.

487
00:49:05,480 --> 00:49:06,720
How is Grandfather?

488
00:49:07,720 --> 00:49:09,160
He hasn't regained consciousness.

489
00:49:14,240 --> 00:49:15,440
Are you Mr. Prajak's family?

490
00:49:17,040 --> 00:49:18,320
Yes.

491
00:49:18,960 --> 00:49:21,320
The doctor needs to discuss something
with you in his office.

492
00:49:22,080 --> 00:49:23,920
-Okay.
-I'll come with you.

493
00:49:39,320 --> 00:49:41,360
Even Aunt Da thinks it's strange.

494
00:49:41,440 --> 00:49:46,160
She says Mr. Prajak is usually healthy.
He's never lost consciousness or fainted.

495
00:49:46,760 --> 00:49:50,080
But after Ms. Pimpa's funeral,
he seemed tired.

496
00:49:50,160 --> 00:49:51,960
And he'd been drinking too.

497
00:49:53,640 --> 00:49:55,200
Are you sure

498
00:49:55,720 --> 00:49:58,840
you were the first to find Mr. Prajak,
not your brother?

499
00:49:59,440 --> 00:50:00,640
What are you trying to say now?

500
00:50:01,400 --> 00:50:03,480
I think you know what I mean.

501
00:50:03,560 --> 00:50:07,080
I don't. And I don't understand

502
00:50:07,160 --> 00:50:09,280
why you care so much about this.

503
00:50:09,800 --> 00:50:12,320
Have you ever asked Korn
these questions to his face?

504
00:50:12,400 --> 00:50:14,520
I'm planning to.

505
00:50:18,480 --> 00:50:22,960
Who knows? Mr. Prajak might already have
Ms. Pimpa's DNA test results.

506
00:50:24,880 --> 00:50:28,160
Was your degree in business
or content creation?

507
00:50:29,320 --> 00:50:32,240
I'm not making this up. There's evidence.

508
00:50:32,320 --> 00:50:34,520
Evidence? What evidence? Tell me.

509
00:50:35,480 --> 00:50:36,600
Forget it.

510
00:50:36,680 --> 00:50:38,200
I don't want to talk to someone so biased.

511
00:50:58,680 --> 00:51:00,480
Here you go.

512
00:51:00,560 --> 00:51:02,200
This bowl's less spicy.

513
00:51:02,720 --> 00:51:03,760
Yay!

514
00:51:05,560 --> 00:51:09,080
It's not often
we all get to be together like this.

515
00:51:10,280 --> 00:51:13,480
Eat plenty, Mom.
Look how thin you've gotten.

516
00:51:15,360 --> 00:51:19,560
You too. You're not
as cheerful as you used to be.

517
00:51:20,760 --> 00:51:23,200
He'll be his old self again soon, Mom.

518
00:51:25,280 --> 00:51:27,840
Korn, don't you have something
to tell Mom?

519
00:51:28,440 --> 00:51:29,440
Go on, tell her.

520
00:51:32,960 --> 00:51:34,160
What is it, Korn?

521
00:51:34,760 --> 00:51:37,800
Um, well…

522
00:51:44,160 --> 00:51:45,160
Well…

523
00:51:46,000 --> 00:51:48,480
I wanted to quit and go back to school.

524
00:51:50,280 --> 00:51:52,520
But I've changed my mind.

525
00:51:52,600 --> 00:51:56,720
Especially with everything going on,
I should stay and help Ms. Nada for now.

526
00:51:58,520 --> 00:51:59,400
Okay.

527
00:52:41,160 --> 00:52:45,240
PROJECT OVERVIEW BEFORE THE BOARD MEETING
NEW PROJECT DESIGNS, CANCEL THE MEETING

528
00:52:54,560 --> 00:52:56,520
No one stays the same forever.

529
00:52:57,480 --> 00:53:00,840
I've grown, and so have you.

530
00:53:01,680 --> 00:53:03,280
Even Ms. Nada has changed.

531
00:53:04,880 --> 00:53:06,160
How?

532
00:53:07,280 --> 00:53:09,680
I've read her diary.

533
00:53:10,240 --> 00:53:13,040
She said her dream
was to open a coffee shop.

534
00:53:13,640 --> 00:53:18,080
But in her latest interview, she said
working for the company was her dream.

535
00:53:19,120 --> 00:53:20,080
See?

536
00:53:21,160 --> 00:53:23,200
Even dreams can change.

537
00:53:24,000 --> 00:53:25,360
Even handwriting.

538
00:53:27,160 --> 00:53:30,600
Her handwriting? Mother's?

539
00:53:32,040 --> 00:53:33,160
Here.

540
00:53:36,080 --> 00:53:39,320
Look. Ms. Nada's handwriting now

541
00:53:39,400 --> 00:53:41,280
looks nothing like it does in her diary.

542
00:53:42,200 --> 00:53:44,160
Times change. People change.

543
00:53:45,040 --> 00:53:46,680
Don't overthink it, Korn.

544
00:53:47,920 --> 00:53:50,240
Let's get something to eat. I'm hungry.

545
00:54:10,560 --> 00:54:14,720
You said you were tired and uneasy
and wanted to come clean and come home.

546
00:54:16,400 --> 00:54:20,560
I've changed my mind. I want to help
Ms. Nada to repay her kindness.

547
00:54:23,640 --> 00:54:26,560
Sorry you got close to Grandfather
for nothing, Wee.

548
00:54:26,640 --> 00:54:28,880
-Korn.
-I'm leaving.

549
00:55:06,840 --> 00:55:08,000
I WANT A LITTLE CAFE OF MY OWN

550
00:55:08,080 --> 00:55:09,440
DECORATED JUST THE WAY I LIKE IT

551
00:55:09,520 --> 00:55:11,240
PROJECT OVERVIEW BEFORE THE BOARD MEETING

552
00:55:14,800 --> 00:55:17,760
The handwriting doesn't match.
Like two different people wrote them.

553
00:55:25,720 --> 00:55:27,680
If Wee is her real son,

554
00:55:29,560 --> 00:55:31,000
who is this woman?

555
00:55:42,960 --> 00:55:46,800
I thought you'd stay over there.
What is it?

556
00:55:49,040 --> 00:55:51,120
I'd like to talk to you, Mother.

557
00:55:56,040 --> 00:55:59,080
Aunt Pim secretly had our blood
tested for DNA.

558
00:56:06,760 --> 00:56:10,120
And I think you've known for a long time

559
00:56:10,720 --> 00:56:12,680
that I'm not your biological son.

560
00:56:14,320 --> 00:56:16,000
But what's even stranger

561
00:56:17,040 --> 00:56:19,640
is why the results show you and Wee

562
00:56:20,600 --> 00:56:22,280
aren't mother and son.

563
00:57:12,720 --> 00:57:14,000
Who are you really?

564
00:57:26,960 --> 00:57:28,240
What do you want?

565
00:57:28,320 --> 00:57:32,480
Legally adopt me. Then we won't need
a DNA test that could expose us.

566
00:57:33,560 --> 00:57:37,760
Are you sure the Phakorn you know
is still the same person?

567
00:57:39,880 --> 00:57:42,880
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">If you love Korn,</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">just say yes and settle it.</font></font></i>

568
00:57:42,960 --> 00:57:45,200
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Don't make his last name a condition.</font></font></i>

569
00:57:46,240 --> 00:57:49,440
If you try anything, I'll get rid of you.

570
00:57:50,040 --> 00:57:51,000
Go ahead.

571
00:57:53,720 --> 00:57:56,640
Your secret won't stay secret anymore.

572
00:58:01,840 --> 00:58:02,880
Korn.

573
00:58:05,200 --> 00:58:07,280
Korn!

574
00:58:07,360 --> 00:58:09,360
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">You keep pretending</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">you're on my side, Wee.</font></font></i>

575
00:58:09,440 --> 00:58:11,760
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">But you're out to stab me in the back,</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">aren't you?</font></font></i>

576
00:58:11,840 --> 00:58:15,080
Or are you jealous
that I have a better life?

577
00:58:54,160 --> 00:58:55,520
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
